### Infrastructure (IaC — AWS ECS Fargate)

This project ships Terraform under `iac/` to deploy to AWS ECS Fargate: an ALB
that path-routes `/api/*`, `/admin/*`, `/django-static/*` to the Django backend
and everything else to the nginx frontend, two Fargate services, RDS PostgreSQL
(credentials in Secrets Manager){{#if withS3}}, an S3 media bucket{{/if}}{{#if withRedis}}, ElastiCache Redis{{/if}}{{#if withCelery}}, a Celery worker service{{/if}}{{#if withCeleryBeat}} and a beat service{{/if}}.
All commands are environment-scoped via `--env` (**required** — no default, to
avoid acting on the wrong environment). Run any command without `--env` to list
environments. State lives in S3, so commands run the same locally and in CI.
See `iac/README.md` for the full workflow.

| Command                 | What it does                                                  |
|-------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| `dude iac login`        | Configure/verify AWS credentials for an environment           |
| `dude iac bootstrap`    | One-time: state backend (S3+DynamoDB) + the two ECR repos     |
| `dude iac new-env --env <name>` | Scaffold a new environment (copies `dev` by default)  |
| `dude iac init`         | `terraform init` (configures the S3 backend for the env)      |
| `dude iac plan`         | `terraform plan`                                              |
| `dude iac apply`        | Provision/update infrastructure (`--yes` to auto-approve)     |
| `dude iac destroy`      | Tear down infrastructure (`--yes` to auto-approve)            |
| `dude iac output`       | Show outputs (app URL, ECR URLs, RDS endpoint; `--json`)      |
| `dude iac build/push/deploy` | Build → push → roll the backend + frontend images        |
| `dude iac ship`         | build + push + deploy in one step (tag = git short SHA)       |
| `dude iac migrate`      | Run `manage.py migrate` as a one-off Fargate task             |
| `dude iac status/logs`  | Service state / CloudWatch logs (`--service backend…`)        |

These commands appear **only** in IaC-enabled projects. Production always runs
PostgreSQL on RDS regardless of the local database choice.
{{/if}}

### Project-local custom commands

This project can define its own `dude` commands under `.dude/commands/`. Each
file becomes a command named after the file (`reset.ts` → `dude reset`); no
registration step. They appear in `dude help` under **PROJECT COMMANDS** and
take precedence over stack commands of the same name (so a `.dude/commands/up.ts`
overrides the default `dude up`). The core commands `init`, `upgrade`, `version`,
and `help` are reserved.

Commands are loaded with [jiti](https://github.com/unjs/jiti), so they can be
written in TypeScript and `import` any package added to the project. Use the
`defineCommand` helper for type-checking:

```ts
// .dude/commands/reset.ts
import { defineCommand } from '@cubocicloide/dude'

export default defineCommand({
  description: 'Reset the database to a clean state.',
  args: { force: { type: 'boolean', description: 'Skip confirmation.' } },
  async run({ projectRoot, args }) {
    // ...
  },
})
```

See `.dude/commands/README.md` (shipped with the scaffold) for the full contract.

