## Tech stack conventions

### Backend (`backend/`)

- **Language**: Python ≥ 3.13
- **Package manager / runtime**: `uv` (never use pip directly)
- **Linter / formatter**: `ruff` — rules `E, F, I, N, UP, B, S, RUF`, line length 100
- **Tests**: `pytest` + `pytest-django`; each app owns its `tests/` package
- **Settings**: split modules — `base.py` (shared), `local.py` (dev), `production.py`
  (deployed); selected via `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE`, values via `django-environ`

**The app pattern** (enforced by `dude lint` — see `.claude/rules/BE/001–014`):

- One Django app per domain under `apps/`, registered in `LOCAL_APPS` (BE001).
- `serializers.py` — explicit `fields` tuples, never `"__all__"` (BE002).
- `views.py` — thin orchestration: explicit `permission_classes` (BE003) and
  `serializer_class`/`@extend_schema` (BE013); **no ORM writes** (BE005).
- `services.py` — all writes/business logic live here, testable without HTTP.
- `models.py` — `__str__` + `Meta.ordering` (BE009), no `null=True` on text
  fields (BE010), explicit `related_name` (BE011); every change ships a
  committed migration (BE006).
- `urls.py` — `app_name` + DRF router, mounted under `/api/` in `config/urls.py` (BE008).
- `tests/` — required for every app (BE014). No raw SQL (BE004), no `print()` (BE012).

### Frontend (`frontend/src/`)

- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Framework**: React 19 with function components + hooks
- **Build tool**: Vite
- **Package manager**: `pnpm`
- **Formatter**: `prettier` (run via `dude format`)
- **Linter**: ESLint with `react-hooks` + `react-refresh` plugins
- **API client**: `frontend/src/openapi/` — **never edit by hand**, always regenerate via `dude api sync`

### Docker Compose

- Service names: `frontend`, `backend`{{#if withPostgres}}, `postgres`{{/if}}{{#if withS3}}, `minio`{{/if}}{{#if withRedis}}, `redis`{{/if}}{{#if withCelery}}, `celery_worker`, `flower`{{/if}}{{#if withCeleryBeat}}, `celery_beat`{{/if}} (use these with `dude logs`, `dude shell`)
- Hot-reload is enabled in development mode for both frontend and backend

